# Cloud generation

Assume empty chat history. Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/video-engine/CLOUD_AGENT_START_PROMPT.md`.

```text
.venv/bin/python -m channel generate --channel <mode> --title "<title>"
.venv/bin/python -m channel drop --channel <mode> --title "<title>"
.venv/bin/python -m channel cloud-readiness
```

Write only under `artifacts/<JOB_ID>/`. Do not clobber repo-root `fixtures/` or another job. Do not commit `.mp4` files.

Normal generation does not edit `channel/config.py`, `*_prompts.py`, or QA thresholds.

Documentary path does not need `FAL_KEY` / `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY`. The engine never calls those APIs. Gemini TTS uses `GEMINI_API_KEY` (`python -m channel tts`, model `gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview`) and saves narration chunks. Opt-in stills use the same key (`python -m channel images`, Nano Banana 2 / `gemini-3.1-flash-image`) and do not run on `--resume`. Opt-in clips use the same key (`python -m channel videos`, `gemini-omni-1.1-flash` image-to-video) and also do not run on `--resume`. Fill research + narration using `MASTER` in the prompt module (same staged loop, DNA per channel), then stop at `WAIT_AUDIO` unless that key is set. After timestamps, Flow prompts in batches of 20 (**Reply "next"**). Drop-folder cuts skip that loop: operator stills named `[00-00]_….jpg` plus audio in `drop/`, then assemble without burned captions.

Costco shipped recuts stay at Kokoro 0.92; new titles stay at spoken **1.0–1.15** (default 1.15) word budget with Gemini TTS or imported audio.
